{"turn_index": 3, "timestamp": 1777553583.1714404, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Onions make you cry because they release a gas when you cut them. It reacts with the water in your eyes.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.009053342044353485, "prediction_error": 5.052918434143066, "progress_signal": -2.0210780700047812, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "time", "morning", "onion", "gas"], "arousal": 0.6714658766967266, "valence": 0.0, "workspace_turn": 4, "threshold": 0.008094205474480986, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 4, "timestamp": 1777553583.5574503, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Salt does more than make food taste salty. It wakes up all the other flavours.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.0112270787358284, "prediction_error": 5.4716033935546875, "progress_signal": -1.934493511915207, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "time", "salt", "morning", "onion"], "arousal": 0.7708913738538778, "valence": 0.0, "workspace_turn": 5, "threshold": 0.009922836720943452, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 5, "timestamp": 1777553583.933519, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "I tried making pasta from scratch once. It was a mess but it tasted better than the boxed kind.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.012037900276482105, "prediction_error": 5.960891246795654, "progress_signal": -2.0368826627731322, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "time", "salt", "morning", "onion"], "arousal": 0.8897693000982355, "valence": 0.0, "workspace_turn": 6, "threshold": 0.011429784120991826, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 6, "timestamp": 1777553584.308429, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Boiling water takes forever when you watch it. Turns out covering the pot actually helps.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.013798975385725498, "prediction_error": 6.203096866607666, "progress_signal": -1.9396078387896223, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "time", "salt", "morning", "onion"], "arousal": 0.9969028177169972, "valence": 0.0, "workspace_turn": 7, "threshold": 0.012214007787406445, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 7, "timestamp": 1777553584.6868656, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Eggs are strange. They can be scrambled, boiled, fried, poached, or baked and they taste completely different each time.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.016297010704874992, "prediction_error": 6.191221237182617, "progress_signal": -1.65064537525177, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "time", "salt", "morning", "onion"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": -0.08266604265123975, "workspace_turn": 8, "threshold": 0.013710921630263329, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 8, "timestamp": 1777553585.0632348, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Ripe bananas are sweeter because the starch converts to sugar as they age.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.017794232815504074, "prediction_error": 6.260303497314453, "progress_signal": -1.5133969634771347, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "time", "salt", "morning", "ripe banana"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": -0.07853274051867776, "workspace_turn": 9, "threshold": 0.015797403641045094, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 9, "timestamp": 1777553585.4410064, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "The crust of bread is just the outside drying out faster in the oven. That's the whole secret.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.02250533364713192, "prediction_error": 5.770159721374512, "progress_signal": -0.8550979693730669, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "time", "bread", "salt", "morning"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": -0.07460610349274387, "workspace_turn": 10, "threshold": 0.017270205076783895, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 10, "timestamp": 1777553585.818591, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Garlic softens when you cook it. Raw garlic is sharp and almost harsh. Roasted garlic is sweet and mellow.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.027618223801255226, "prediction_error": 5.126582145690918, "progress_signal": -0.12601059675216675, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "time", "sweet", "bread", "salt"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": -0.07087579831810667, "workspace_turn": 11, "threshold": 0.020149783231317997, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 11, "timestamp": 1777553586.2007473, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "I always let the pan heat up before adding oil. My dad taught me that. I don't actually know why it works, it just does.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.029361460357904434, "prediction_error": 4.534280776977539, "progress_signal": 0.7931964159011837, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "time", "sweet", "bread", "salt"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": -0.06733200840220133, "workspace_turn": 12, "threshold": 0.024294845201075076, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 12, "timestamp": 1777553586.5782518, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Soup tastes better the next day. The flavours have more time to mix together.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.033511362969875336, "prediction_error": 3.6612493991851807, "progress_signal": 1.8037868499755856, "top_5_concepts": ["time", "water", "sweet", "bread", "flavour"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": -0.06396540798209126, "workspace_turn": 13, "threshold": 0.027966871112585067, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 13, "timestamp": 1777553586.9585092, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Chocolate melts at body temperature. That's not an accident. It's part of why it feels good to eat.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.03397854417562485, "prediction_error": 3.0421698093414307, "progress_signal": 2.381060862541199, "top_5_concepts": ["time", "water", "sweet", "bread", "flavour"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": -0.06076713758298669, "workspace_turn": 14, "threshold": 0.029568955488502975, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 14, "timestamp": 1777553587.3426187, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Ice cream gets icier over time because small ice crystals merge into bigger ones. Eating it fast is actually the right call.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.032986417412757874, "prediction_error": 2.5015480518341064, "progress_signal": 2.7206077575683594, "top_5_concepts": ["time", "water", "sweet", "bread", "flavour"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": -0.05772878070383736, "workspace_turn": 15, "threshold": 0.03262392170727253, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 15, "timestamp": 1777553614.9837394, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "I forgot to add sugar to my cookies once and didn't notice until they came out pale and flat.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.03014177456498146, "prediction_error": 2.252021074295044, "progress_signal": 2.6731292009353638, "top_5_concepts": ["time", "water", "sugar", "sweet", "bread"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": -0.05210022458521321, "workspace_turn": 17, "threshold": 0.03227525670081377, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 16, "timestamp": 1777553615.3724227, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Rice needs to rest after cooking. Lifting the lid too soon lets the steam out and the grains go sticky.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.02600494958460331, "prediction_error": 1.9509414434432983, "progress_signal": 2.6033218145370487, "top_5_concepts": ["time", "water", "sugar", "sweet", "bread"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": -0.04949521335595255, "workspace_turn": 18, "threshold": 0.031848560273647304, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 17, "timestamp": 1777553615.7593234, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Lemons and limes are interchangeable in most recipes but they have a different sharpness. Limes are a bit more bitter.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.021714676171541214, "prediction_error": 2.0221962928771973, "progress_signal": 2.106851422786713, "top_5_concepts": ["time", "water", "sugar", "sweet", "lemon"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": -0.04702045268815492, "workspace_turn": 19, "threshold": 0.031421863846480845, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 18, "timestamp": 1777553616.139372, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Frying makes food crispy because the water inside turns to steam and escapes. The outside dries and browns.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.02020215429365635, "prediction_error": 1.761169672012329, "progress_signal": 1.950975549221039, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "time", "sugar", "food", "sweet"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": -0.04466943005374717, "workspace_turn": 20, "threshold": 0.030995167419314382, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 19, "timestamp": 1777553616.5217679, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "The smell of baking bread is mostly from compounds called esters. Your nose is reacting to chemistry, not magic.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.019155796617269516, "prediction_error": 1.7075763940811157, "progress_signal": 1.55465544462204, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "time", "bread", "smell", "sugar"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": -0.04243595855105981, "workspace_turn": 21, "threshold": 0.03056847099214792, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 20, "timestamp": 1777553616.9033933, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Butter burns faster than oil because it contains milk solids. Clarified butter removes those and handles heat better.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.018284237012267113, "prediction_error": 1.4647222757339478, "progress_signal": 1.391251230239868, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "time", "bread", "smell", "oil"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": -0.04031416062350682, "workspace_turn": 22, "threshold": 0.03014177456498146, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 21, "timestamp": 1777553617.281571, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "I chop onions under cold water to stop my eyes burning. It mostly works.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.01698298193514347, "prediction_error": 1.5348883867263794, "progress_signal": 0.9548991322517395, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "time", "bread", "onion", "eye"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": -0.03829845259233147, "workspace_turn": 23, "threshold": 0.030024727433919905, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 22, "timestamp": 1777553617.6623883, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Tea steeps faster in hotter water. But some teas get bitter if the water is too hot. Green tea is fussy that way.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.014287653379142284, "prediction_error": 1.4287235736846924, "progress_signal": 0.7611247062683106, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "time", "bitter", "bread", "onion"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": -0.0363835299627149, "workspace_turn": 24, "threshold": 0.029907680302858352, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 23, "timestamp": 1777553618.0463269, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Milk left on the counter for a few hours smells fine but will make you sick. Some things spoil before they smell.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.013825526461005211, "prediction_error": 1.342915654182434, "progress_signal": 0.6236800432205201, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "time", "bitter", "milk", "bread"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": -0.03456435346457915, "workspace_turn": 25, "threshold": 0.0297906331717968, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 24, "timestamp": 1777553618.4229062, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Pasta water is salty for a reason. It seasons the pasta from inside while it cooks.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.012865482829511166, "prediction_error": 1.1729918718338013, "progress_signal": 0.6236784100532531, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "time", "bitter", "milk", "bread"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": -0.032836135791350196, "workspace_turn": 26, "threshold": 0.029673586040735243, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 25, "timestamp": 1777553618.8032827, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "I find making food for other people more satisfying than making it just for myself. I don't fully understand why.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.012940040789544582, "prediction_error": 1.1969949007034302, "progress_signal": 0.46681976318359375, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "food", "time", "bitter", "milk"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.05453171449085451, "workspace_turn": 27, "threshold": 0.02955653890967369, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 26, "timestamp": 1777553619.1851215, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Steak rested for a few minutes after cooking stays juicier. The fibres relax and reabsorb the moisture.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.01298021711409092, "prediction_error": 1.237186312675476, "progress_signal": 0.3211257338523865, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "food", "time", "bitter", "milk"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.051805128766311784, "workspace_turn": 28, "threshold": 0.029439491778612135, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 27, "timestamp": 1777553619.565752, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Honey never goes bad. They found edible honey in Egyptian tombs. Low water content stops bacteria growing.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.010056308470666409, "prediction_error": 1.1299591064453125, "progress_signal": 0.35697742700576773, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "honey", "food", "time", "bitter"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.04921487232799619, "workspace_turn": 29, "threshold": 0.029274298530071973, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 28, "timestamp": 1777553619.9465294, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Caramel is just sugar heated past its melting point. But the window between golden and burnt is about thirty seconds.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.00836457684636116, "prediction_error": 1.0812042951583862, "progress_signal": 0.31650851964950566, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "honey", "caramel", "sugar", "food"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.04675412871159638, "workspace_turn": 30, "threshold": 0.029012813046574593, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 29, "timestamp": 1777553620.3266225, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "The first bite of something is always the most intense. Your brain adapts fast and the second bite is already less.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.009682813659310341, "prediction_error": 1.132792353630066, "progress_signal": 0.1969239234924316, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "second", "honey", "caramel", "sugar"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.044416422276016554, "workspace_turn": 31, "threshold": 0.02875132756307721, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 30, "timestamp": 1777553620.7105935, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Spicy food doesn't actually burn you. Capsaicin tricks the same nerve receptors that respond to heat. Your body believes the lie.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.009830842725932598, "prediction_error": 1.0992356538772583, "progress_signal": 0.17300221920013437, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "food", "second", "honey", "caramel"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.042195601162215726, "workspace_turn": 32, "threshold": 0.02848984207957983, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 31, "timestamp": 1777553621.0901213, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "I always make too much pasta. Measuring it dry is harder than it looks.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.008147796615958214, "prediction_error": 0.9814616441726685, "progress_signal": 0.2542275667190552, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "food", "pasta", "second", "honey"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.04008582110410494, "workspace_turn": 33, "threshold": 0.028228356596082447, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 32, "timestamp": 1777553621.4721744, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Fermentation is controlled rot. Cheese, yogurt, bread, beer, pickles \u2014 all of them involve letting the right bacteria win.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.007987084798514843, "prediction_error": 1.0144648551940918, "progress_signal": 0.1658816814422608, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "food", "bread", "bacteria", "pasta"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.03808153004889969, "workspace_turn": 34, "threshold": 0.027966871112585067, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 33, "timestamp": 1777553621.8514125, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Cold butter makes flaky pastry. Warm butter makes it dense. Temperature is doing most of the work in baking.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.009752405807375908, "prediction_error": 1.0866996049880981, "progress_signal": 0.052221059799194336, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "food", "bread", "bacteria", "pasta"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.036177453546454706, "workspace_turn": 35, "threshold": 0.027705385629087687, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 34, "timestamp": 1777553622.2329948, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Apples and avocados go brown when you cut them because oxygen reacts with the exposed flesh. Lemon juice slows it down.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.00749405100941658, "prediction_error": 1.0047247409820557, "progress_signal": 0.10857431888580327, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "food", "bread", "bacteria", "pasta"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.03436858086913197, "workspace_turn": 36, "threshold": 0.02745689637959003, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 35, "timestamp": 1777553622.6128635, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "I cook rice by absorption now. I measured it out for years before I trusted my eyes and ears to tell me when it was done.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.008290408179163933, "prediction_error": 1.0379233360290527, "progress_signal": 0.0585490107536315, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "food", "bread", "bacteria", "eye"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.03265015182567537, "workspace_turn": 37, "threshold": 0.027214905247092247, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 36, "timestamp": 1777553622.9950318, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "The Maillard reaction is what makes browned food taste better than just cooked food. It's a chemical reaction between sugars and proteins.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.0062155574560165405, "prediction_error": 0.8518807888031006, "progress_signal": 0.22868440151214608, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "food", "sugar", "bread", "bacteria"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.0310176442343916, "workspace_turn": 38, "threshold": 0.026972914114594456, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 37, "timestamp": 1777553623.3783586, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Strawberries lose flavour quickly after picking. The ones at the market have usually been travelling for days.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.006641543935984373, "prediction_error": 0.9677712321281433, "progress_signal": 0.07426340579986568, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "food", "sugar", "bread", "bacteria"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.029466762022672018, "workspace_turn": 39, "threshold": 0.026730922982096672, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 38, "timestamp": 1777553623.763631, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "A sharp knife is actually safer than a dull one. Dull knives slip. Sharp knives go where you aim them.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.006369008682668209, "prediction_error": 1.108473300933838, "progress_signal": -0.08265745043754569, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "food", "sugar", "bread", "bacteria"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.027993423921538415, "workspace_turn": 40, "threshold": 0.02648893184959888, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 39, "timestamp": 1777553624.1464112, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "I keep forgetting to put things in the fridge. Not because I forget \u2014 I just don't want the cooking to be over.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.006730963010340929, "prediction_error": 0.9336302280426025, "progress_signal": 0.09491252303123465, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "food", "sugar", "cooking", "thing"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.02659375272546149, "workspace_turn": 41, "threshold": 0.026246940717101094, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 40, "timestamp": 1777553624.5254188, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Vinegar and baking soda fizz because one is an acid and one is a base. The bubbles are carbon dioxide.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.00635216711089015, "prediction_error": 0.919520914554596, "progress_signal": 0.08910562396049504, "top_5_concepts": ["water", "food", "sugar", "cooking", "thing"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.025264065089188416, "workspace_turn": 42, "threshold": 0.02600494958460331, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 41, "timestamp": 1777553624.9075031, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Food cooked slowly at low heat tastes different from food cooked fast at high heat. Both are valid, they just produce different things.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.00596718629822135, "prediction_error": 1.033589243888855, "progress_signal": -0.04293417930603027, "top_5_concepts": ["food", "water", "thing", "sugar", "low"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.024000861834728993, "workspace_turn": 43, "threshold": 0.025480007193982607, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 42, "timestamp": 1777553625.2888231, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "I once made soup entirely from leftovers and it was better than most things I planned.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.0064003183506429195, "prediction_error": 0.9424546360969543, "progress_signal": 0.05341318845748899, "top_5_concepts": ["thing", "food", "water", "sugar", "low"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.022800818742992543, "workspace_turn": 44, "threshold": 0.024955064803361876, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 43, "timestamp": 1777553625.6680963, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Salt in sweet things is not a mistake. A pinch of salt in chocolate or caramel makes the sweetness more noticeable.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.006326335947960615, "prediction_error": 0.9844170212745667, "progress_signal": 0.004249781370162964, "top_5_concepts": ["thing", "food", "water", "caramel", "sugar"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.021660777805842916, "workspace_turn": 45, "threshold": 0.024430122412741173, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 44, "timestamp": 1777553626.0490787, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Garlic burns in about forty-five seconds if the pan is too hot. After that the whole dish tastes bitter.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.00518277520313859, "prediction_error": 0.8089252710342407, "progress_signal": 0.1695132732391358, "top_5_concepts": ["thing", "food", "water", "caramel", "second"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.02057773891555077, "workspace_turn": 46, "threshold": 0.02390518002212047, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 45, "timestamp": 1777553626.4381554, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Resting dough relaxes the gluten. That's why bread dough is easier to shape after it sits for a while.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.005886323284357786, "prediction_error": 1.0379836559295654, "progress_signal": -0.07912505865097041, "top_5_concepts": ["thing", "food", "bread", "water", "caramel"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.01954885196977323, "workspace_turn": 47, "threshold": 0.023380237631499767, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 46, "timestamp": 1777553626.82013, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "I like cooking alone. The kitchen is where I think most clearly.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.005818416830152273, "prediction_error": 0.8098778128623962, "progress_signal": 0.14898681640625, "top_5_concepts": ["thing", "food", "bread", "water", "caramel"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.018571409371284566, "workspace_turn": 48, "threshold": 0.022855295240879064, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 47, "timestamp": 1777553627.205166, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Olive oil has a smoke point lower than most frying oils. It's better for finishing and dressing than for high heat.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.0055963704362511635, "prediction_error": 0.8969792723655701, "progress_signal": 0.05768505930900569, "top_5_concepts": ["thing", "food", "heat", "bread", "water"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.017642838902720337, "workspace_turn": 49, "threshold": 0.02246580077335238, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
{"turn_index": 48, "timestamp": 1777553627.5827625, "autonomous_question_fired": false, "question_used": null, "input": "Onions cooked slowly for forty minutes become something completely different. Caramelised onions barely resemble raw ones.", "epistemic_uncertainty": 0.005721844732761383, "prediction_error": 0.9369351267814636, "progress_signal": 0.010650008916854858, "top_5_concepts": ["thing", "food", "heat", "bread", "water"], "arousal": 1.0, "valence": 0.01676069695758432, "workspace_turn": 50, "threshold": 0.022347202152013777, "has_questions": false, "response_integrated": false, "domain": "everyday"}
